 "result": "Start in `src/tessel/sessions.py`.\n\n- **Lines 57–80, `SignedCookieSession`**: it extends `CallbackDict`, and `on_update` sets `self.modified = True` only when a top-level key is set or deleted. `session['cart']['items'].append(x)` mutates a nested object in place, so `on_update` never fires and `modified` stays `False`.\n- **Line ~245, `should_set_cookie`**: it returns `session.modified or (session.permanent and SESSION_REFRESH_EACH_REQUEST)`. With `modified` false, `save_session` (~line 352) skips writing the cookie, and the change is lost on the next request.\n\n**Fixes:**\n- Set `session.modified = True` after nested mutations (the standard workaround).\n- Reassign the key, e.g. `session['cart'] = cart`.\n- Wrap nested values so they propagate changes. This is a design change, so I'd only do it if you want the library to handle nested mutation itself.\n\nIf the app uses a custom session interface (check `tests/test_session_interface.py` and `app.py` for `session_interface`), the same `modified` logic applies there.",
